  "id": "adaptive-testing",
  "term": "adaptive testing",
  "definition": "Adaptive testing is a computer-based way of giving a series of rigorously reviewed questions that can be adjusted as the assessment proceeds rather than only using a fixed short form. In this context, it is used to collect precise patient-reported information about physical, mental, and social well-being and to generate reports about quality of life and treatment effects.",
